7	 Browsers create or join a private match by a six-character code and sail placeholder ships around the slice sea: a compact map with four small islands with docks, reefs and shoal walls that funnel every route between islands through one central crossing, and eight outer-sea spawn slots. Up (or W) sails ahead, down (S) brakes and then reverses, left and right (A, D) turn, and E docks a ship beside a dock, at any speed. The authoritative server decides every position and sends each browser only the ships within its sight radius; the minimap's fog clears where the player has sailed.
8	 
9	-The combat spike (§18 stage 1) runs beside it: "Create duel" makes a 1v1 duel whose code the second browser enters under "Join duel", and "Practice" fights a server-side dummy (idle or guarding). After a three-second countdown both browsers predict the fight with the shared duel simulation and roll back to the server's inputs (`docs/duel.md`). Keys (§8): WASD or the arrows move (hold back to guard), J light, K heavy, U and I specials, Shift dash, J and K together throw. The HUD shows both health bars, stamina, the round clock, the connection line (round trip, input delay, corrections) and the result; "Show hitboxes" draws hurtboxes and active hitboxes.
10	+Fights happen at sea (§6): J grapples the nearest ship ahead within six tiles. The attacker sees its aim, the target a warning with the side it comes from, and it lands after a one-second windup unless the target sails out of range or out of the aim (a miss costs six seconds). A grapple that lands stops both ships; after a three-second countdown the two fight the online duel inside the match, in the same page's arena, while everyone else in sight sees crossed swords and the elapsed time where they fight. The winner sails on with eight seconds of protection; the loser respawns at a dock 15 seconds after the fight, with 20 seconds of protection; a draw returns both to separate nearby points. A fighter who drops has ten seconds to come back to the same fight; leaving forfeits.
11	+
12	+The standalone duel (the combat spike, §18 stage 1) runs beside it: "Create duel" makes a 1v1 duel whose code the second browser enters under "Join duel", and "Practice" fights a server-side dummy (idle or guarding). After a three-second countdown both browsers predict the fight with the shared duel simulation and roll back to the server's inputs (`docs/duel.md`). Keys (§8): WASD or the arrows move (hold back to guard), J light, K heavy, U and I specials, Shift dash, J and K together throw. The HUD shows both health bars, stamina, the round clock, the connection line (round trip, input delay, corrections) and the result; "Show hitboxes" draws hurtboxes and active hitboxes.
